  pages    = "56--69",
  abstract = "Spatial equity is an important component of sustainable urban
              planning. We introduce an Integrated Spatial Equity Evaluation
              (ISEE) framework based on spatial multi-criteria analysis to
              assess spatial equity. This framework measures the balance between
              demands generated by residential areas and supply offered by urban
              services at various spatial scales. It considers the balance
